# The Home page's tiles: the Home Assistant entities worth a lamp.
#
# Copy this file to <config>/project-dashboard/home-tiles.conf and edit it
# (<config> is $SYSTEM_TOOLS_CONFIG, default ~/.config/system); the lines below
# are examples. Entity ids describe a house, so the real list stays outside
# the checkout. Without a home-tiles.conf the page shows no tiles and says why.
#
# Pipe-separated, one tile per line, in the order the page draws them:
#
#   headline|<entity_id>|<name>[|<type>]          the lamp above the groups
#   tile|<group>|<entity_id>|<name>[|<type>]      a tile in its group
#
# <type> is optional: alarm, lock, toggle or sensor, how the tile reads its
# state. Without it the domain decides; a virtual binary sensor that works as
# a switch says toggle. A tile's commands follow its domain: the Home Assistant
# services the dashboard allows for it (home_screen.SERVICES).
#
# The page reads each tile's state and its age from Home Assistant, with the
# URL and token local-ha-mcp uses (<config>/ha-mcp/.env); a tile it cannot read
# names why; a script or automation shows its last run. A light, switch, fan or input_boolean turns on and off with Undo; a scene, script or button runs once;
# a lock, alarm or cover asks for its entity id typed out first. Any other domain gets Read state, a curl line for
# Copy only. A line the page cannot read is named on the page and skipped.

headline|binary_sensor.problems_active|Problems active

tile|Security|alarm_control_panel.house|House alarm
tile|Security|lock.front_door|Front door
tile|Water & safety|binary_sensor.water_leak|Water leak
tile|Water & safety|binary_sensor.smoke_sensors|Smoke sensors
tile|Network & backup|binary_sensor.wan_degraded|WAN degraded
tile|Network & backup|sensor.backup_last_successful_automatic_backup|Last automatic backup
tile|Toggles|input_boolean.guest_mode|Guest mode
tile|Toggles|binary_sensor.virtual_porch_light|Porch light|toggle
